@page
@using ForestChurches.Pages.Docs
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = "Admin.Read")]
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Whitelisting, sign-up and sign-in – Website administrator guide";
}

<header>
    <p class="fc-eyebrow">Website administrator guide · Technical reference</p>
    <h1>Whitelisting, sign-up and sign-in</h1>
    <p class="docs-lead">How the invitation whitelist works, what happens at each step of registration, how email links are protected, and how sign-in, two-factor and sessions work.</p>
    <div class="docs-meta"><span>Code: <code>Pages/Admin/Invite</code>, <code>Components/UserRegistration</code>, <code>Areas/Identity/Pages/Account</code>, <code>Components/Security</code></span></div>
</header>

<h2>Why there's a whitelist</h2>
<p>Anyone who registers gets a church listing that's immediately public and can receive messages from visitors. To stop spam and impersonation, registration is closed to everyone except email addresses an administrator has added to the <code>WhitelistedUsers</code> table (shown in Site admin as <strong>Invitations</strong>).</p>

