<h3>Step by step</h3>
<ol class="docs-steps">
    <li><strong>Invite.</strong> <code>Invite.OnPostAddWhitelistedUser</code> adds a <code>WhitelistedUsers</code> row (<code>Status = "Pending"</code>, <code>ExpiryDate = now + 24 h</code>). <code>RegistrationGenerate.GenerateUrl</code> builds <code>/Identity/Account/register?email=…</code> and also resets the expiry of every row for that email to now + 24 h.</li>
    <li><strong>Invitation email.</strong> <code>MailSender.SendEmailInviteUser</code> wraps the register URL in a <em>callback token</em> valid for 1 day (see below) and hands the <code>registration_invite</code> template to the email app.</li>
    <li><strong>Opening the link.</strong> <code>/ValidateToken?token=…</code> decrypts the token; if it's valid and not expired it redirects to the register page, otherwise it shows an "expired or invalid" page.</li>
    <li><strong>Registering.</strong> <code>Register.OnPostAsync</code> accepts the form only if:
        <ul>
            <li>the email is in the whitelist (<strong>exact, case-sensitive match</strong>, because the check compares against an in-memory list of whitelisted emails), and</li>
            <li><code>ValidateEmail</code> finds the first whitelist row for that email with <code>Status = "Pending"</code> and an expiry in the future, and</li>
            <li>the password passes the password rules.</li>
        </ul>
        Otherwise it shows "Email is already registered or the registration has expired".
    </li>
    <li><strong>Account and listing.</strong> It creates the <code>ChurchAccount</code> (unconfirmed, no roles), a <code>ChurchInformation</code> row with placeholders (<em>Default Church</em>, address <em>TBA</em>, every facility on, <strong>Status = Open</strong>) and stores the uploaded logo (or the default <code>IMGUR-1.png</code>) in blob storage. The whitelist row becomes <code>Completed</code> with the registration date.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirmation.</strong> An Identity email-confirmation token is generated (valid <strong>2 hours</strong>, <code>DataProtectionTokenProviderOptions.TokenLifespan</code>); the user ID and code are protected with the <code>fc.data.url.email</code> protector and sent in <em>Confirm your account</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirming.</strong> <code>ConfirmEmail</code> confirms the account and adds the <code>AuthorizedChurch</code> role. Sign-in requires a confirmed account (<code>RequireConfirmedAccount = true</code>).</li>
</ol>

<div class="docs-callout docs-callout--warn">
    <span class="docs-callout__title">Things to know</span>
    <ul>
        <li>New listings are <strong>Open</strong> (public) as soon as the account is created, even before email confirmation, with placeholder details.</li>
        <li>Sending the same invitation twice creates duplicate rows. Only the first row for an email is checked and completed.</li>
        <li>Removing an invitation doesn't affect an account that already exists.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend link</strong> extends the expiry but doesn't reset a <code>Completed</code> row back to <code>Pending</code>.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

